{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q410654","formula":"Cl₃Dy","hill":"Cl3Dy","elements":["Cl","Dy"],"composition":{"Cl":3.0,"Dy":1.0},"names":{"en":"Dysprosium chloride","ru":"Хлорид диспрозия(III)"},"descriptions":{"en":"Dysprosium(III) chloride (DyCl3), also known as dysprosium trichloride, is a compound of dysprosium and chlorine. It is a white to yellow solid which rapidly absorbs water on exposure to moist air to form a hexahydrate, DyCl3·6H2O. Simple rapid heating of the hydrate causes partial hydrolysis to an oxychloride, DyOCl.","ru":"Хлорид диспрозия(III) — неорганическое соединение, соль диспрозия и соляной кислоты с формулой DyCl3, бесцветные кристаллы, хорошо растворяется в воде, образует кристаллогидрат. Относится к группе химических соединений трихлоридов лантаноидов с формулой LnCl3, где Ln обозначает металл-лантаноид."},"fame":20,"pubchemCid":66207,"mass":268.85,"charge":0,"smiles":"Cl[Dy](Cl)Cl","inchikey":"BOXVSFHSLKQLNZ-UHFFFAOYSA-K","iupac":"trichlorodysprosium","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"crystal","source":"materialsproject","ref":"mp-28448","atoms":24,"license":"CC BY 4.0, Materials Project"},"structure":{"cell":[[3.786,0.0,0.0],[0.0,12.217,0.0],[0.0,0.0,8.517]],"kind":"crystal","atoms":[{"x":0.0,"y":2.962,"z":6.388,"el":"Dy"},{"x":3.786,"y":2.962,"z":6.388,"el":"Dy"},{"x":1.893,"y":3.147,"z":2.129,"el":"Dy"},{"x":1.893,"y":1.111,"z":6.388,"el":"Cl"},{"x":0.0,"y":4.998,"z":2.129,"el":"Cl"},{"x":3.786,"y":4.998,"z":2.129,"el":"Cl"},{"x":0.0,"y":1.846,"z":3.682,"el":"Cl"},{"x":3.786,"y":1.846,"z":3.682,"el":"Cl"},{"x":1.893,"y":4.262,"z":4.835,"el":"Cl"},{"x":1.893,"y":4.262,"z":7.941,"el":"Cl"},{"x":0.0,"y":1.846,"z":0.577,"el":"Cl"},{"x":3.786,"y":1.846,"z":0.577,"el":"Cl"},{"x":1.893,"y":9.07,"z":6.388,"el":"Dy"},{"x":0.0,"y":9.256,"z":2.129,"el":"Dy"},{"x":3.786,"y":9.256,"z":2.129,"el":"Dy"},{"x":0.0,"y":7.219,"z"